@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+# AArch64 sprite kernels
+
+The HLE PPU's sprite mask and shift operations use eight-byte AArch64 NEON
+vectors when `__aarch64__` and `__ARM_NEON` are present. Existing x86-64 SSE2
+and portable implementations remain available. `NESRECOMP_PPU_HLE_FORCE_PORTABLE`
+forces the scalar reference, including on ARM. No architecture header is
+included on an unrelated target.
+
+The kernel loads exactly eight lanes, tests counters before decrementing,
+uses unsigned saturating counter subtraction and shifts only ready sprite
+planes. A weighted horizontal reduction packs the eight high bits into the
+existing priority mask. The HD recorder's shift mask retains the same meaning.
+No guest clock, bus access, mapper behavior, save field or game routine changes.
+
+`cyc_ppu_kernel_test` compares native/scalar operations over every planar row,
+all simultaneous lane masks, all byte-valued counters at every lane and 250,000
+random configurations, including rendering-off and skipped-dot cases.
+`cyc_ppu_span_reference` now explicitly forces portable kernels, so its complete
+machine comparison also checks SIMD against scalar processing. Native interval
+and raster interval tests continue to pass.
+
+Two supplied games retain their 1,800-frame traces, native/interpreter parity,
+state continuation, untraced pixels, PCM and PNG. A separate MesenCE PAL capture
+matches 903 consecutive first-level frames after pre-input boot calibration.
+SDK GCC-generated kernel objects also pass the pure-kernel test under ARM64
+Linux with a test-only assertion bridge; that checks generated instructions,
+not libnx lifecycle or physical-console performance.
+
+Balanced Mac measurements show about 4.80% less process CPU for the tested PAL
+route. Mario's 1.09% result falls inside its A/A noise and is not a demonstrated
+desktop speedup. Switch Cortex-A57 performance still needs measurement. These
+kernels are a shared optimization, not a full-speed or visual-glitch fix claim.
